{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1763017,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"indigo-dark_un","paid":0,"title":"CaseQuest","festival_id":507505,"organization_id":113323,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-01T18:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-12-30T21:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/casequest-strategia27-the-annual-business-strategy-fest-of-loyola-college-loyola-college-lc-chennai-1763017","region":"hybrid","details":"<p><strong>CaseQuest<\/strong> is a <strong>business strategy<\/strong> and <strong>case-study competition, in Strategia'27<\/strong>&nbsp;that brings together sharp analytical thinking, decision-making under pressure, and live presentation skills, testing participants across a series of progressively challenging rounds.<\/p>\n<p>The competition begins with a <strong>two-part online qualifier<\/strong>, followed by a live branching case-study round, and concludes with a <strong>Grand Finale<\/strong> where the top teams present a brand-new case before a judging panel.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Participants will be evaluated on:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Depth of analysis<\/li>\n<li>Clarity and structure of explanation<\/li>\n<li>Quality of decision-making<\/li>\n<li>Awareness of Trade-Offs and Risks<\/li>\n<li>Ability to adapt strategy&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Consistency of decisions&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Guidelines:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to all registered UG\/PG students.<\/li>\n<li>Every round is played in teams of exactly 2 members - individual participation is not allowed at any stage.<\/li>\n<li>Both members register together, and the same two-member team continues across all rounds; changes are allowed only in exceptional cases, at the Organizing Committee's discretion.<\/li>\n<li>Carry a valid institutional ID card at all times - it may be checked at any stage.<\/li>\n<li>Use of AI tools (ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, Copilot, etc.), internet search, or unauthorized notes\/textbooks is strictly banned unless a round specifically allows it.<\/li>\n<li>Teams may only communicate with their own teammate - contact with other teams or outside help is not permitted.<\/li>\n<li>Only the materials explicitly permitted for a round may be used; all other devices and references are prohibited.<\/li>\n<li>Only responses submitted in the official format\/portal are evaluated - loose sheets or unofficial submissions are not considered.<\/li>\n<li>Once submitted, responses are final and cannot be edited or resubmitted.<\/li>\n<li>Violations such as AI use, plagiarism, impersonation, or unauthorized assistance lead to immediate disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>Decisions of the Judges and Organizing Committee on evaluation, rules, and disputes are final and binding - no re-evaluation requests are entertained after results are declared.<\/li>\n<li>The Organizing Committee may revise rules, format, or schedule if required, and will inform all participants in advance.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Stages &amp; Timelines:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><em><strong>Stage 1: Online Qualifier (Dec'26)<\/strong><\/em><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Date: TBA<\/strong><\/li>\n<li><strong>Time: TBA<\/strong><\/li>\n<li><strong>Duration: TBA<\/strong><\/li>\n<li><strong>Platform: Unstop<\/strong><\/li>\n<li><strong>Guidelines<\/strong>: A two-part quiz that narrows the full field of registered teams down to the 50 teams who advance to Stage 2.\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Part A - General Round (Current Affairs &amp; Business Awareness):&nbsp;<\/strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to<strong> all registered teams<\/strong>. Questions cover general current affairs together with foundational business and economic awareness.<\/li>\n<li>All registered teams compete in Part A.<\/li>\n<li>Each part includes a mix of regular questions and Star Questions - Star Questions carry bonus\/higher marks than regular questions.<\/li>\n<li>Scored on total marks earned (regular + Star Questions); the top teams (by cumulative score) advance to Part B.<\/li>\n<li>Ties are broken by time taken to complete the round - the faster team is ranked higher.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li><strong>Part B - Advanced Business Round:<\/strong>\n<ul>\n<li>A more in-depth quiz restricted to the <strong>top teams<\/strong> who cleared Part A, testing deeper business, finance, and industry knowledge.<\/li>\n<li>Open only to the teams that qualify from Part A.<\/li>\n<li>As in Part A, a mix of regular questions and higher-value Star Questions is used; Star Questions carry bonus marks.<\/li>\n<li>Scored on total marks earned (regular + Star Questions); the top 50 teams (by cumulative score) advance to Stage 2.<\/li>\n<li>Ties are broken by time taken to complete the round - the faster team is ranked higher.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><em><strong>Stage 2: The Case Study Round (15 Feb'27):<\/strong><\/em><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The centrepiece of the event. Teams work through a live, branching business case and are evaluated on the judgment behind every decision - not just the decisions themselves.<\/li>\n<li>The<strong> Stage 2 case is released to the qualifying teams only once Stage 1<\/strong> (Parts A and B) has concluded and the qualifying teams are confirmed.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Format:<\/strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Each case presents a company facing a real-world business challenge.<\/li>\n<li>Each case consists of four sequential decision points. At every stage, participants choose one of the available strategic options.<\/li>\n<li>The case follows a branching format - the option selected at each decision point determines the scenario and question presented next. Different teams may therefore encounter different paths through the same case.<\/li>\n<li>At each decision point, teams must select one option, and justify the decision using logical reasoning, relevant business concepts, and practical considerations.<\/li>\n<li>Once a decision is made at any stage, it is final and cannot be changed. Teams must continue the case based on the consequences of their previous choice.<\/li>\n<li>Reasonable assumptions are permitted where necessary - they must be clearly stated and must align with the information given in the case.<\/li>\n<li>Answers should be concise, focused, and directly relevant to the case facts; unrelated theory without practical application may not receive marks.<\/li>\n<li>There is no single correct path or perfect answer - each option carries its own advantages and limitations.<\/li>\n<li>Strong, well-supported reasoning is rewarded regardless of the path chosen; selecting an option without adequate justification receives limited marks even if the decision itself was appropriate.<\/li>\n<li>At the conclusion of the case, each team presents and justifies its complete sequence of decisions to the judges - explaining the rationale behind their strategy and how their choices addressed the evolving business challenge.<\/li>\n<li>Top teams (by cumulative score) advance to Stage 3, the Grand Finale.<\/li>\n<li>The decision of the evaluators is final and binding.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><em><strong>Stage 3: Grand Finale (16 Feb'27) :<\/strong><\/em><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Held on Day 2 of the event - the final 25 teams receive a brand-new case study and present their analysis live before the judging panel.<\/li>\n<li>A new case study, not seen in Stage 2, is introduced exclusively for the Grand Finale.<\/li>\n<li>Finalist teams work through the new case and prepare their strategic recommendation and supporting reasoning.<\/li>\n<li>Each team then presents and defends its analysis and decisions live before the judges.<\/li>\n<li>Judges may question teams on their assumptions, trade-offs, and the consistency of their overall strategy.<\/li>\n<li>Case format, preparation time, presentation time per team, and the final marking scheme: to be finalized by the Organizing Committee.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Think Strategically. Decide Boldly. Win the Case.<\/strong><\/p>","overall